Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.52,0:00:05.27,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Go on.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.98,0:00:11.42,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Focus on expanding your senses.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.42,0:00:14.95,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You can break a spell by severing \Nits linchpin, even with a regular sword.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.73,0:00:26.84,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I feel like I've gotten the hang of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.84,0:00:28.42,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,Your Majesty! Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.58,0:00:32.50,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,You've a letter from Princess Nephelli!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.50,0:00:34.09,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Directly from Nephelli?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.23,0:02:11.98,Ep Title,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,1)}~ Unseen Visage ~
Dialogue: 0,0:02:13.06,0:02:17.65,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,It seems the prime minister of Yarda \Nis trying to oust the crown prince, Savas.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.02,0:02:21.87,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,Which is why Princess Nephelli wants \Nto stay in Farsas for the time being.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.87,0:02:25.96,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Well, turning her away would come off \Nas unnatural, so I've replied with a "yes."
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.96,0:02:27.44,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,Of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.44,0:02:30.58,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,Your Majesty's on good terms \Nwith Princess Nephelli.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.08,0:02:33.39,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Will it be okay with Tinasha here?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.39,0:02:35.30,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,We can't have her making enemies with Yarda.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.30,0:02:37.51,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,I believe that's in your hands...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.51,0:02:39.89,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I'll warn her the next time I see her.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.89,0:02:43.00,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Though she seems busy \Nbreaking my curse lately.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.00,0:02:45.35,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,Your Majesty, please act \Nwith the utmost prudence.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.35,0:02:47.43,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I'll mention it during our training.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.93,0:02:50.44,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,If I talk to her outdoors, \Nshe can't break any windows.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.44,0:02:52.52,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,That's not what I meant.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:52.52,0:02:55.27,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,There's less than a month until her coronation.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.27,0:02:57.00,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,She'll handle it just fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.00,0:02:59.15,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,That's just how the two of us are built.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.65,0:03:05.32,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,That singing...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.32,0:03:06.60,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,It's Tinasha.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.60,0:03:09.80,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,I hear someone in the palace got married,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.80,0:03:12.03,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,and they're holding a wedding banquet.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.85,0:03:14.44,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,She sure is talented.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.06,0:03:17.93,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I'll make an appearance later.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.48,0:03:29.95,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Congratulations on getting married.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.69,0:03:38.91,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Huh? Oscar?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.91,0:03:40.68,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You know this is alcoholic.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.68,0:03:42.51,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What? But it's sweet.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.51,0:03:44.03,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,It's sweet {\i1}and{\i0} alcoholic.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.32,0:03:45.61,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.61,0:03:49.32,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,When I get drunk, my magic \Ngoes a little out of control.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.95,0:03:51.50,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,That's no good.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:51.50,0:03:53.01,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I swear...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.01,0:03:55.96,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Put on sealing ornaments. \NThis is a festive occasion.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.96,0:03:57.51,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.30,0:04:01.99,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Hold on, lemme try again.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.53,0:04:08.51,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It's a cat.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.51,0:04:09.66,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Yeah, I can tell!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.23,0:04:14.61,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Stop using magic!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.61,0:04:15.69,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,Your Majesty!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.69,0:04:17.56,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,We've received a reply from Yarda.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.56,0:04:19.85,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,The princess should arrive in two days.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.36,0:04:23.70,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Got it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.70,0:04:25.30,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Please make the necessary arrangements.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.30,0:04:27.23,Default,Lazar,0,0,0,,C-Certainly.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.69,0:04:31.29,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Oscar, are you gonna get married?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.29,0:04:33.91,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Not sure. Why do you ask?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.10,0:04:37.25,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,If you've got something to say, out with it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.25,0:04:41.23,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,No, I'm just here to be of use to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.23,0:04:43.22,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Marry whoever you like.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.82,0:04:46.09,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Sure thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.09,0:04:49.18,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I'll find a queen who doesn't \Nbreak the palace windows.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.72,0:04:53.73,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I hate you!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.73,0:04:56.94,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,And I hate mages who can't hold their liquor.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.94,0:04:59.38,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You big fat dummy!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.09,0:05:12.14,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I liked your singing, though.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.83,0:05:20.34,Default,Nephelli,0,0,0,,I apologize for my sudden intrusion.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.64,0:05:24.30,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I'm sure staying in an unfamiliar land \Nisn't easy, but please enjoy your stay.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.87,0:05:28.26,Default,Nephelli,0,0,0,,Thank you so much for your generosity.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.27,0:05:34.81,Default,Nephelli,0,0,0,,I believe the princess of Tuldarr \Nis here as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.81,0:05:37.06,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Yes, I'll have her say hello.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.06,0:05:40.73,Default,Nephelli,0,0,0,,Prince Legis introduced me to her before.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.73,0:05:42.78,Default,Nephelli,0,0,0,,I must say, she's beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.78,0:05:45.49,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,She's like a powder keg.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.49,0:05:48.96,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,An intense personality, \Nand I don't care much for her looks.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.49,0:06:02.03,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It's been a long time, Princess Nephelli.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.03,0:06:04.41,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'm honored to see you again.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.70,0:06:08.72,Default,Nephelli,0,0,0,,I could say the same thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.72,0:06:11.26,Default,Nephelli,0,0,0,,I hear it's not too long \Nuntil you ascend the throne.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.26,0:06:14.87,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Things have been hectic for me, \Nso please forgive my lack of courtesy.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.74,0:06:36.76,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You should defend with your magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.76,0:06:39.15,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,No, that wouldn't be fair.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.92,0:06:44.12,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Good afternoon.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.12,0:06:45.42,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Out on a stroll?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.42,0:06:47.63,Default,Nephelli,0,0,0,,I was hoping to get some light exercise.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.63,0:06:50.59,Default,Nephelli,0,0,0,,Princess Tinasha, \Ndo you two always spar like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.59,0:06:53.53,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Yes, I'm having him train me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.14,0:06:59.94,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Disperse.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.86,0:07:05.04,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Where's it coming from?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.04,0:07:06.22,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'll find out.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.22,0:07:07.25,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Mila.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.25,0:07:08.57,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,Yes, ma'am!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.57,0:07:10.24,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Go after the assassin.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.24,0:07:11.49,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Keep him alive, if possible.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.49,0:07:13.12,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,If not, feel free to kill him.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.12,0:07:14.53,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,Right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.01,0:07:19.13,Default,Nephelli,0,0,0,,U-Um, what's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.13,0:07:22.04,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Looks like an assassin made it \Nthrough the palace barrier.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.04,0:07:25.50,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I think they escaped, \Nbut it'd be best to go back inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.22,0:07:31.93,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It's safe to say their target \Nwas Princess Nephelli.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.93,0:07:35.14,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,However, this man is just a hired hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.42,0:07:39.10,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Having just a hired hand break \Nthrough the barrier is still a problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.98,0:07:44.77,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,The barrier prevents \Nunauthorized teleportation from outside,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.77,0:07:47.32,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,but you can still enter on foot.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.32,0:07:50.78,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,So he had someone's help \Nfrom within the palace?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.09,0:07:52.52,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Als, make him talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.52,0:07:53.77,Default,Als,0,0,0,,As you wish.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.33,0:07:55.21,Default,Als,0,0,0,,Get up!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.24,0:07:58.07,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What a hassle.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.07,0:08:00.60,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Even if the Yarda prime minister \Nis implicated here,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.60,0:08:02.22,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,that's an issue for their nation.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.22,0:08:05.23,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,The most I can do is \Nlet them know what happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.23,0:08:08.64,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You could get involved \Nif you were engaged to their princess.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.64,0:08:10.94,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Get engaged just for that?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.94,0:08:12.47,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,That's a big leap of logic.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.47,0:08:19.21,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,An engagement would give you just cause \Nto meddle in their affairs to an extent.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.21,0:08:22.43,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Don't you think that's the reason \Nshe came here to begin with?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.43,0:08:24.69,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Thus the assassin, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.69,0:08:28.90,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,If Nephelli dies, there'd be no risk \Nof me poking my nose into Yarda.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.26,0:08:33.75,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Having the princess die in Farsas \Nwould let them blame you as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.07,0:08:41.04,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Oscar sure is friendly \Nwith the princess of Yarda.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.04,0:08:44.21,Default,Mila,0,0,0,,If she bothers you that much, \Nwhy not just kill her?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.21,0:08:45.80,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'm not doing that!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.20,0:08:49.21,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Travis.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.21,0:08:50.89,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Aw, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.89,0:08:52.21,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Just murder her.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.21,0:08:53.80,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Giving into temptation is easier.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.22,0:08:56.01,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You again?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.01,0:08:58.01,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What do you want this time?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.01,0:09:00.63,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,I'm bored, so I came to laugh at you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.26,0:09:03.61,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,The prince of Yarda is a timid one.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.61,0:09:06.73,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Unlike the prime minister, \Nwho's quite remarkable.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.73,0:09:08.19,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Is that right?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.52,0:09:10.97,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,He's willing to make small \Nsacrifices for the big picture,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.97,0:09:14.15,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,and he does whatever it takes \Nfor a quick resolution.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.15,0:09:16.41,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,And how do you know that?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.41,0:09:18.87,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Because I'm currently in Gandona.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.87,0:09:23.12,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'm aware that Gandona \Nborders both Farsas and Yarda,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.12,0:09:25.33,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,but does that have anything to do with you?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.33,0:09:26.92,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Sure it does.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:27.37,0:09:30.29,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,I'm acting as the guardian \Nto the heir to Gandona's throne.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.29,0:09:31.56,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.56,0:09:34.76,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Well? Feel like killing that princess yet?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.05,0:09:39.22,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Don't you think you should \Nmake better use of your powers?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.22,0:09:42.40,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,People are defined by more than their power.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.40,0:09:44.93,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,What's wrong with using what you've got?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.93,0:09:47.39,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,That man is what you're after, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.37,0:09:52.27,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You can't win people over by killing others.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.76,0:09:58.45,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,So be it, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.45,0:10:02.72,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,That aside, an insect has made \Nits way into this castle, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.72,0:10:04.65,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You mean the assassin?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.65,0:10:08.58,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I feel sorry for the princess, having \Nsomeone after her even in a foreign nation.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.91,0:10:10.32,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Not that.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.32,0:10:11.79,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,A different insect.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.79,0:10:12.60,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.40,0:10:16.17,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,Enjoy your fruitless efforts.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.17,0:10:20.62,Default,Travis,0,0,0,,You'll be left in the lurch if you place \Ntoo much confidence in your abilities.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.62,0:10:23.06,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,What do you mean, "left in the lurch?"
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.19,0:10:27.75,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Seriously, what's his deal?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.12,0:10:35.53,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,{\i1}The king of Farsas hinted at the fact \Nthat there may be a spy hiding in our midst.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.86,0:10:38.95,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,{\i1}Her Highness had assumed \Nwe were all trustworthy,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.47,0:10:42.92,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,{\i1}and now she's practically \Nconfined herself to her room.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.78,0:10:45.12,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Is something wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.12,0:10:46.58,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,Oh, Valt.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.93,0:10:50.20,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,I can't believe an assassin is after her \Nall the way here in Farsas.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.20,0:10:52.93,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,I was thinking we might have \Nbeen better off in Yarda.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.93,0:10:55.80,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,We stand a better chance here in Farsas.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.80,0:11:00.96,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,And I'm sure the king of Farsas will prove \Nto be a strong ally for Her Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.96,0:11:04.26,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,We might even see a partnership \Nbetween our countries in the future.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.26,0:11:08.03,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,Well, I'm sure Her Highness would be happy—
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.97,0:11:09.81,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.86,0:11:19.32,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,She met her end while \Ntasting the soup for poison.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.32,0:11:21.70,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It's a commonplace potion.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.03,0:11:27.10,Default,Kumu,0,0,0,,A number of others ate the soup \Nin question, but they were all fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.10,0:11:29.66,Default,Kumu,0,0,0,,No potions were detected in the soup pot.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.95,0:11:33.39,Default,Als,0,0,0,,The meal was brought by a lady-in-waiting \Nand an officer from Yarda.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.39,0:11:36.00,Default,Als,0,0,0,,That officer has now gone missing.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.00,0:11:39.26,Default,Als,0,0,0,,The lady-in-waiting claims that \Nhe handed her the food.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.26,0:11:41.72,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,He's so suspicious, it's almost funny.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.72,0:11:45.93,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,That officer's name is Eneas, \Nand he was close with both ladies-in-waiting.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.93,0:11:49.68,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,That is how I believe \Nhe was able to pull this off.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.64,0:11:53.52,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,I understand it's a lot to ask,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.01,0:11:57.61,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,but could you please assist \NPrincess Nephelli in this time?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.61,0:12:00.45,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I will be more vigilant, of course,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.45,0:12:02.32,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,and I intend to find the culprit.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.32,0:12:03.95,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,Thank you very much,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.60,0:12:06.76,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,but that's not what I meant.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.76,0:12:11.57,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,Princess Nephelli has had an interest \Nin you since ten years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.57,0:12:12.84,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,If it's possible—
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.84,0:12:13.79,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I understand.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.17,0:12:16.00,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I'll do what I can.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.42,0:12:24.82,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Feel like poking your nose in?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:24.82,0:12:26.26,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I'm left with no choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.54,0:12:28.47,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,In that case, I'll help.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.47,0:12:29.76,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Are you sure?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.76,0:12:31.84,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Don't you have to prepare for your coronation?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.84,0:12:34.52,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I have Legis lending me his support.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.52,0:12:35.73,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Sorry about this.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.73,0:12:37.78,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I want to settle this matter before you leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:38.70,0:12:42.65,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Incidentally, breaking your curse \Nshould take about two more weeks.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:43.16,0:12:44.45,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.45,0:12:45.86,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,And you won't mess up?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.86,0:12:48.22,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Don't be mean like that!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.00,0:12:57.44,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You're...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.44,0:12:59.45,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,My name is Valt, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.96,0:13:02.47,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You're suppressing your magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.88,0:13:07.80,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,In truth, your magic exceeds that \Nof a nation's chief mage.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:07.80,0:13:09.98,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I wouldn't go that far.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.98,0:13:16.77,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,That said, most of my magic is acquired, \Nso I'd rather not have others know about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.05,0:13:22.73,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,So have you come to me because \Nyou have clues to the assassin's identity?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.73,0:13:25.56,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,No, that's not it.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.56,0:13:28.95,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I was hoping you could answer a question \NI had about spell compositions.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.95,0:13:29.75,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.64,0:13:35.95,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I can't thank you enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.95,0:13:39.58,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Oh, no, it served as a good \Nchange of pace for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.93,0:13:43.95,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Now I can return to guarding \NPrincess Nephelli with no reservations.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.95,0:13:48.55,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,The king of Farsas said he'll cooperate, \Nso the engagement should be any day now.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.55,0:13:49.43,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.35,0:13:52.89,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Yarda is acting like they're engaged already.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.89,0:13:57.98,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Those two have always been close, \Nso I'm sure they'll make a happy couple.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.50,0:14:02.04,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,So now you can finally be free, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.60,0:14:07.01,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Please take care,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.01,0:14:08.73,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Queen of Tuldarr.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.01,0:14:13.29,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Free...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.26,0:14:19.22,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Who that man marries is none of my business.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.79,0:14:35.81,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Are you feeling all right, Princess Nephelli?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.81,0:14:38.27,Default,Nephelli,0,0,0,,Thank you for your concern.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.27,0:14:42.73,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I apologize that I must return \Nto Tuldarr in the middle of our search.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.73,0:14:44.35,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Are you leaving right now?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.35,0:14:46.44,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,No, I still have some time.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.44,0:14:49.65,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Then why not regale us \Nwith a song before leaving?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.34,0:14:51.67,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,A song?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.73,0:15:05.25,Narration,Song,0,0,0,,Manifold colors bathed in light
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.25,0:15:10.54,Narration,Song,0,0,0,,Drifting unknown to all
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.54,0:15:13.62,Narration,Song,0,0,0,,The shadows of time
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.62,0:15:21.33,Narration,Song,0,0,0,,Carried away in the wind
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.33,0:15:26.30,Narration,Song,0,0,0,,Twilight recedes away
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.30,0:15:33.24,Narration,Song,0,0,0,,As remnants of a dream diverge
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.19,0:15:41.96,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,With that, I'll be taking my leave.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.19,0:15:45.20,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Nephelli.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.20,0:15:46.12,Default,Nephelli,0,0,0,,Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.12,0:15:47.21,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Tomorrow...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.54,0:15:49.77,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Why don't we go out for some fresh air?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.76,0:15:57.98,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You wouldn't want to get sunburned.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.98,0:16:00.60,Default,Nephelli,0,0,0,,Th-Thank you!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.42,0:16:10.00,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I don't think you'd get lost, \Nbut stay close to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.00,0:16:11.96,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,We'll reach a lake at the end of this forest.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.13,0:16:29.53,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.53,0:16:30.58,Default,Nephelli,0,0,0,,Gait!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.58,0:16:31.71,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,Are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.05,0:16:36.64,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,Lucanos! Valt!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.64,0:16:38.10,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,Watch our surroundings!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.41,0:16:40.80,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,Your Highness, let's return \Nto the palace for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.80,0:16:42.05,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,I'll open a teleportation portal.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.05,0:16:42.90,Default,Nephelli,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.90,0:16:45.06,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,Your safety is our top priority.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.95,0:16:55.49,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,So you're the one?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.39,0:16:57.45,Default,Lucanos,0,0,0,,It can't be!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.37,0:17:01.83,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.79,0:17:07.01,Default,Gait,0,0,0,,Wh-Where's Her Highness?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.01,0:17:09.29,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,She's with Oscar.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.29,0:17:12.74,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You confused the two of us because \Nof my curse song from last night.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.17,0:17:16.59,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Although it didn't seem to work on one of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.34,0:17:20.06,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,It's too late to back down.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.37,0:17:23.64,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Did you kill the officer who went missing?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.64,0:17:25.84,Default,Lucanos,0,0,0,,Damn you!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.45,0:17:42.96,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Time to tell us whose orders \Nyou've been acting on.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.37,0:17:45.33,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Go on, before you die.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.18,0:17:59.08,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Oscar!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.08,0:18:00.82,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Why won't you use your magic?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.82,0:18:02.14,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Are you an idiot?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.37,0:18:14.22,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I made it in time thanks to your teleport.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.22,0:18:15.32,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.32,0:18:16.74,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,Think nothing of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.74,0:18:19.01,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,I can't have her dying here.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.01,0:18:21.74,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,So why's he still moving?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.74,0:18:24.70,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,He must have swallowed \Na seed with a forbidden curse.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.98,0:18:28.34,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,It activates when one receives a mortal wound,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.34,0:18:31.47,Default,Valt,0,0,0,,bestowing upon them power \Nthat exceeds physical limits.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.47,0:18:32.48,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.48,0:18:33.78,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,And you end up with {\i1}that{\i0}.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.10,0:18:37.06,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Oscar.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.06,0:18:39.59,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Can you see the magic stagnating within him?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.03,0:18:43.49,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Kind of.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.49,0:18:47.33,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I see faint white lines like the veins \Nof a leaf across his entire body.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.33,0:18:50.52,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,The linchpin is the part where \Nhis magic is visibly concentrated.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.52,0:18:54.67,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I see where it is, but a stab there \Nwould normally kill someone.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.67,0:18:58.57,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Do that, and I'll keep him alive \Nso he can at least be interrogated.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.97,0:19:00.49,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Don't get any more injuries.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:09.70,0:19:12.25,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Now you belong to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:18.15,0:19:20.37,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Now you can finally return \Nto your home country.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.37,0:19:22.29,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You've gone through so much here.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.29,0:19:23.85,Default,Nephelli,0,0,0,,N-No...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.79,0:19:28.31,Default,Nephelli,0,0,0,,King Oscar...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.33,0:19:32.49,Default,Nephelli,0,0,0,,Do you remember my \Nproposal from ten years ago?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.21,0:19:48.37,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,From the ceasefire agreement?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.37,0:19:49.36,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I do.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.15,0:19:56.99,Default,Nephelli,0,0,0,,If I asked you to marry me now, \Nlike I did ten years ago, would you say yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.84,0:19:59.94,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Let me see.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.36,0:20:05.50,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Should it turn out to benefit both of us, \NI'll be the one to submit an offer.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.22,0:20:09.12,Default,Nephelli,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.73,0:20:14.90,Default,Nephelli,0,0,0,,Thank you very much for all of your help.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.72,0:20:20.90,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Are you sure it's okay \Nto let Princess Nephelli leave?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.90,0:20:23.63,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,There's no reason for her to stay any longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.63,0:20:25.37,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,I'm sure she's keen to leave as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.37,0:20:27.94,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,But I thought you two...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.41,0:20:40.36,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,In that case, can I stay here a little longer?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.92,0:20:42.45,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Whatever suits you best.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.45,0:20:44.63,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Until you become queen, that is.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.96,0:20:46.76,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What's wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.10,0:20:49.89,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,I'm here to follow up on the Yarda matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.89,0:20:51.86,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,There was something that caught my eye.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.47,0:20:55.81,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,Wasn't there a second mage, other than Gait?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.65,0:20:57.96,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,You mean Valt?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.96,0:21:02.28,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,The thing is, we found no records \Nof him in Yarda's royal court.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.28,0:21:03.26,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.26,0:21:06.60,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,Gait and the princess said that he'd \Njoined the court five years ago,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.60,0:21:10.33,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,but it seems that was a false memory \Nthat had been temporarily planted.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:10.33,0:21:12.82,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,So where's Valt now?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.82,0:21:14.41,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,We've already lost track of him.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.84,0:21:18.92,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,Actually, his appearance closely matches \Nthe mage from Delilah's testimony.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.92,0:21:21.78,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,The mage who had ties to that cult?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.13,0:21:24.33,Default,Doan,0,0,0,,If the two are one and the same...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:24.72,0:21:27.87,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,That would mean Valt was the one \Nwho poisoned Tinasha.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.87,0:21:30.68,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,So why did he help us this time around?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.83,0:21:32.86,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,Yes... why?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:33.39,0:21:35.74,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Investigate this further.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:35.74,0:21:39.78,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Whatever agenda he may have, \Ndon't let him get away with anything else.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.28,0:21:43.42,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,Don't worry about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.88,0:21:46.57,Default,Oscar,0,0,0,,You just focus on what you need to do.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.26,0:21:53.10,Flashback,Valt,0,0,0,,So now you can finally be free, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.36,0:21:57.73,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I'll be fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.73,0:22:01.21,Default,Tinasha,0,0,0,,I came here to be of use to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.47,0:23:40.02,Next Ep Title,Sign,0,0,0,,{\fad(500,1)}~ Returning the Promise ~
